post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'

  readcube-wine installs the application on FIRST RUN, not now.

  Papers' licence does not permit repackaging, so the upstream installer is
  shipped verbatim and executed unmodified the first time you run `readcube`.
  Expect a few minutes and roughly 1.5 GB under:

      ~/.local/share/readcube/wineprefix

  Papers is proprietary software from Digital Science. Your use of it is
  governed by the ReadCube Terms of Use:

      https://about.readcube.com/terms/

  A ReadCube account is required to sign in.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}

post_remove() {
    cat <<'EOF'

  The per-user Wine prefix was left in place. To remove it as well:

      rm -rf ~/.local/share/readcube

EOF
}
